# Fantasy General II  (Steam appid 1025440)
#
# ✅ PLAYS (2026-10-02): opening video plays, game runs, and EXIT IS CLEAN
# (Steam's gameprocess_log: Launcher.exe and FG2.exe both "exit code 0").
#
# It needed GStreamer in the runtime, not anything game-specific. Before that,
# the Unity player spun one core at 100% forever after Quit: its video shutdown
# loop (~VideoPlaybackMgr -> ReleaseVideoPlayback) only removes a playback
# whose IsMediaInfoReady() is true, and the teaser FG2_Teaser_01.mp4 (H.264 +
# AAC) could never get there without a Media Foundation decoder. Full write-up
# in docs/NOTEBOOK.md (session 2026-10-01). Reproduced 3/3 before the fix.
#
# Long sessions used to end in "msync: warn: node memory pool exhausted" and
# every core busy: a wait-registration leak in CodeWeavers' msync, which this
# game's threads hit millions of times. Fixed by patches/wine-0007 (2026-10-03;
# a long session after the fix: in_use flat at ~230). docs/NOTEBOOK.md section 7.
#
# Measured on the first launch, 2026-10-01: Steam -> Launcher.exe -> FG2.exe
# all ran; FG2.exe had DXMT's d3d11/dxgi and both winemetal halves mapped;
# output_log.txt reports "Direct3D 11.0 [level 11.1]", Apple M1 Max.
#
#   engine        Unity 2018.4.24f1
#   exe           FG2.exe -- PE32+ x86_64, the Unity player (creates the D3D device)
#   launcher      Launcher.exe -- PE32 .NET, what Steam's default launch option
#                 starts; it then starts FG2.exe. Needs Wine Mono.
#   graphics      Direct3D 11 (store page: "DirectX: Version 11"; Unity's
#                 Windows default, boot.config does not force another API)
#   steam_appid   none shipped -- a *-direct.env profile needs one (RUNTIME.md §9)
#   size          2.9 GB
#
# Steam launch options (appinfo): option 0 = FG2.exe, beta "preview" only;
# option 2 = Launcher.exe, the default for everyone else.

RUNTIME="winecx-26.3.0-sse-x86_64"
PREFIX="steam-winecx"

# D3D11, so wined3d cannot run it on this platform (RUNTIME.md §10). BACKEND=
# alone does not reach a Steam-launched game; the per-app key does, and it is
# keyed on FG2.exe -- the exe that creates the device, NOT the launcher:
#
#   bin/backend-install dxmt-0.80-winecx-26.3.0-sse steam-winecx \
#       winecx-26.3.0-sse-x86_64 --app 'FG2.exe' --app-only
BACKEND="dxmt-0.80-winecx-26.3.0-sse"

EXE='C:\Program Files (x86)\Steam\steam.exe'
WORKDIR="$PREFIXES_DIR/steam-winecx/drive_c/Program Files (x86)/Steam"

ARGS="-applaunch 1025440"

PROFILE_ENV=(
    "WINEDEBUG=${WINEDEBUG--all}"
)

WINEDLLOVERRIDES=""
